        "content": "**Spring AI** is a Spring project for building AI-powered Java applications using familiar Spring conventions. It provides portable abstractions over major AI providers and vector databases, reducing vendor-specific integration code.

### Key capabilities

- **Model APIs:** Chat, text, image, audio transcription, and text-to-speech models.
- **Multiple providers:** Integrations for providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Amazon Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Ollama, and others.
- **`ChatClient`:** A fluent API for prompts, responses, streaming, advisors, and structured output.
- **Tool calling:** Lets models invoke Java methods or external services to retrieve data or perform actions.
- **Structured output:** Maps model responses into Java records/classes.
- **RAG support:** Retrieval-Augmented Generation using document readers, embedding models, vector stores, and retrieval advisors.
- **Vector databases:** Integrations with stores such as PostgreSQL/PGvector, Redis, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, Pinecone, Milvus, and others.
- **Conversation memory:** Maintains message history across interactions.
- **Observability:** Integrates with Spring Boot Actuator and Micrometer for metrics and tracing.
- **Spring Boot integration:** Auto-configuration and starters make provider setup largely configuration-driven.
- **MCP support:** Support for the Model Context Protocol, enabling applications to expose or consume tools and resources.

A typical application configures a provider starter and API key, injects a `ChatClient`, and sends prompts:

```java
@RestController
class AiController {

    private final ChatClient chatClient;

    AiController(ChatClient.Builder builder) {
        this.chatClient = builder.build();
    }

    @GetMapping("/ai")
    String generate(@RequestParam String message) {
        return chatClient.prompt()
                .user(message)
                .call()
                .content();
    }
}
```

Spring AI is particularly useful when you want to combine generative AI with existing Spring Boot services, data access, security, configuration, and observability while keeping model-provider coupling relatively low.

Official documentation:

- [Spring AI Reference Documentation](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/)
- [Spring AI project page](https://spring.io/projects/spring-ai)
